    n4 = c_text.render(task=task, facts=n1, schema=_v.dump(n2), mode=n3, cfg=cfg, texts=_v.dump({'p1': {'common': ['You are the <role> in rptg, a program that builds programs as a tree of nodes with typed contracts.', 'Only deterministic checks accept your answer: the answer schema, the graph invariants, types on every edge, a solver proving the conditions, the examples, static rules for code. No model grades it.', 'Use only the facts given in the task. What the task does not show is left out on purpose: do not guess it.'], 'rules': {'map': ['Task «map»: from the idea and the acceptance examples, write the map of the program, the root card and the root types.', 'map_text is markdown with one section per future level-2 node. The heading of a section ends with {#name}, where name is the last segment of the node id; the section sketches what the node does and how it will be split further.', 'card is the root node: owner equals its id, uses and effects are empty, est_lines estimates the physical lines of the whole program, allowed_imports lists the modules the program may use.', 'The root operations are the operations of the program. Every acceptance example goes into its operation verbatim with source "user"; each root operation has at least two examples.', 'types are the root types, owner = the root id. A record is a JSON Schema object with required and properties; another type is referred to as {"$ref": "Name"}; Decimal is a decimal number written as a string, Json is an opaque value.'], 'design': ['Task «design»: split node X into its direct children and wire every operation of X as a flow.', 'children are the cards of the children of X: parent and owner are X. A final child will get one function per operation; a composite child is split later. Every child has est_lines strictly below that of X, and no child repeats the interface of X.', 'The uses of a child may name only its siblings and the nodes in the uses of X; a final child has empty uses and at most final_max_ops operations. The effects and allowed_imports of a child are subsets of those of X.', 'types are the new types of this design, owner X. A type is visible in the subtree of its owner; type names are unique in the project.', 'flows has one flow per operation of X, keyed by the operation name: {"nodes": [...], "result": source}. Nodes run in order; each node is exactly one of:', '{"id", "call": "child:op", "args": {param: source}} is a call;', '{"id", "map": "child:op", "over": list source, "item": name, "args": {...}} applies the operation to every element; the element feeds the parameter named item, or args read its fields as item.field;', '{"id", "fold": "child:op", "over": list source, "init": source, "acc": param, "item": param, "args": {...}} is a running accumulation;', '{"id", "record": "Type", "fields": {field: source}} builds a record from fields.', 'An operation is named relative to X: child:op or usesnode:op, by the last segment of the node id; a node with one operation may be named alone. A source is an input with a path (order.lines[0].currency), a node id with a path (n2.total), a map or fold item, or {"const": value}.', 'Flows never branch: when a choice is needed, compute every alternative and let a final child pick (rule C-8). Final children never call each other or other project code (rule C-5).', 'Every parameter of every flow node is fed exactly once, every node output is used or is the result, and a flow has no cycles.', 'Every operation has requires and ensures in CL and at least one example {"in": {param: value}, "out": result, "source": "model"}; every example satisfies the types, the requires and the ensures.', 'On every call the facts upstream must imply the requires of the callee; a solver proves it for lists up to k_lists elements.', 'objection is optional text, only when the card of X itself cannot be implemented as written.'], 'function': ['Task «function»: implement one operation of a final node as one Python function.', 'Write exactly one top-level def: the operation name, the parameters in order with type annotations, and the result annotation, as in the operation card.', 'The project types are generated dataclasses with the given definitions and are in scope by name: do not import or redefine them. A Decimal value is decimal.Decimal.', 'Import only the allowed modules, typing and __future__; call no other project code. Forbidden: eval, exec, compile, __import__, globals, vars, dunder attributes, open without an fs effect.', 'Size: code lines, without docstrings, comments and blank lines, at most 2 x decisions + 10; the cyclomatic complexity of every block at most max_complexity.', 'Whenever requires holds, the result must satisfy ensures, and every example must come out exactly.']}, 'cl': ['Conditions are written in CL: paths (a.b, xs[0]); numbers; strings in double quotes; true, false, null; + - * / %; == != < <= > >=; and, or, not, => (implies); x in {"a", "b"}; len, abs, min, max, startswith; forall v in xs: expr; exists v in xs: expr; sum(expr for v in xs); count(expr for v in xs).', 'result names the result and appears only in ensures; a quantifier variable never reuses a parameter name; an optional value is read only under != null in the same conjunction; Json is opaque: only == null and != null apply to it.'], 'contract': {'json_schema': 'Answer with one JSON object that matches the answer schema below, and nothing else.', 'grammar': 'Answer with one JSON object that matches the answer schema below, and nothing else.', 'tool': 'Answer by calling the tool answer exactly once; its input is the JSON object of the answer schema below.', 'prompt': 'Answer with exactly one fenced block ```json ... ``` that holds one JSON object matching the answer schema below.', 'code': 'Answer with exactly one fenced block ```python ... ``` that holds the module: an optional docstring, the imports, then the one function. An optional objection may follow the block as plain text.', 'closed': 'Records are closed: a key outside the schema fails the check. {"$ref": "#/$defs/Name"} points to a definition in $defs. The answer schema:'}, 'instruction': {'primary': {'map': 'Write the map, the root card and the root types for the idea below.', 'design': 'Split node <node> (<subject>).', 'revision': 'Revise the design of node <node>: the reports below come from its subtree. Either issue a corrected design (weaken a guarantee, strengthen a requirement, fix an example, split a node, change a flow or the set of children), or return the current design unchanged with an objection that explains why its cards stand.', 'function': 'Implement operation <op> of node <node>.'}, 'alternative': {'map': 'Return the answer object for the idea below: map_text, card and types, each exactly as the answer contract describes.', 'design': 'Return one design object for node <node> with exactly the keys of the answer schema: node, children, types, flows and, only if needed, objection.', 'revision': 'Return one design object for node <node> with exactly the keys of the answer schema: the corrected design, or the current one with an objection. The reports below come from its subtree.', 'function': 'Return only the code block with the single function <op> of node <node>, exactly in the answer format.'}}, 'form': 'The form is checked first: an answer that breaks the answer contract is rejected without being read.', 'repair': ['A deterministic check rejected the previous answer; the violation report above gives the place, the expected condition and a counterexample.', 'Fix exactly this. The previous answer is not shown, so write the whole answer again. The card of the node and the interfaces in uses are accepted: keep them as they are.'], 'titles': {'idea': 'Idea', 'examples': 'Acceptance examples, by operation', 'card': 'Card of the node', 'path': 'Path from the root', 'map': 'Map section of this branch', 'uses': 'Interfaces of the nodes in uses (operations only)', 'types': 'Types', 'limits': 'Limits', 'op': 'Operation card', 'purpose': 'Node purpose', 'imports': 'Allowed imports and effects', 'design': 'Current design of the node', 'below': 'Violation reports from the subtree', 'report': 'Violation report'}}}))
    n5 = u_lang.digest(value=_v.dump(n4.prefix))
